03:47:14.460 --> 03:47:18.520
is in this recipe for chicken with cashew nuts and a spicy sauce.

03:47:19.510 --> 03:47:24.230
The rules that govern what a proper Chinese recipe should be go back for thousands of years.

03:47:24.710 --> 03:47:28.050
They're really a search for the right balance and contrast.

03:47:28.620 --> 03:47:29.820
And in the area of texture,

03:47:30.000 --> 03:47:31.800
The Chinese are the absolute masters.

03:47:32.390 --> 03:47:35.350
A good example is this recipe for chicken with cashews.

03:47:35.890 --> 03:47:39.510
The chef at Taipei's region hotel heats a little water in a wok.

03:47:39.970 --> 03:47:44.350
Then in goes a half cup each of bamboo shoots, celery, carrots, and mushrooms.

03:47:44.880 --> 03:47:46.320
They cook for a minute and are drained.

03:47:47.000 --> 03:47:49.240
The wok is cleaned and some oil goes in.

03:47:49.610 --> 03:47:52.050
The cashew nuts are fried for 15 seconds.

03:47:52.680 --> 03:47:58.080
A boneless, skinless chicken breast cut into bite-sized pieces cooks in the oil for 30 seconds.

03:47:58.530 --> 03:47:59.710
The wok is cleaned out.

03:48:00.000 --> 03:48:06.160
And in goes a quarter cup each of sliced green onion and red pepper, plus a few tablespoons of garlic.

03:48:06.820 --> 03:48:08.120
The other vegetables return.

03:48:08.870 --> 03:48:11.030
A tablespoon of Chinese chili paste.

03:48:11.410 --> 03:48:11.970
The chicken.

03:48:12.460 --> 03:48:14.080
A teaspoon of sesame oil.

03:48:14.680 --> 03:48:18.860
A half teaspoon of cornstarch mixed into a little water to thicken things up.

03:48:19.560 --> 03:48:20.680
Cashew nuts come back.

03:48:21.220 --> 03:48:23.840
Everything heats up for another half minute, and it's ready.

03:48:24.830 --> 03:48:28.710
Chinese food is probably the most well-traveled cuisine in the world.

03:48:29.250 --> 03:48:29.970
As a matter of fact...

03:48:30.000 --> 03:48:35.870
Chinese food has been available on a high level to so many people in so many cities around the

03:48:35.870 --> 03:48:41.470
world that there has been very little interest in Chinese home cooking except in the Chinese

03:48:41.470 --> 03:48:48.100
communities. But in 1960, all that began to change. Since then, there has been an increasing

03:48:48.100 --> 03:48:54.300
interest in Chinese home cooking in the Western home kitchens. Our supermarkets offer all of the

03:48:54.300 --> 03:48:58.980
basics in terms of Chinese ingredients, and there are really only a few items that are needed in

03:48:58.980 --> 03:48:59.920
the area of condiments.

03:49:00.340 --> 03:49:04.160
Chili sauce or paste made from crushed, fresh chili peppers.

03:49:04.160 --> 03:49:06.220
It'll last for a year in the refrigerator.

03:49:06.890 --> 03:49:10.810
Hoisin sauce, made from soybeans, flour, sugar, salt, and garlic.

03:49:11.290 --> 03:49:14.370
Gives food a sweet, peppery flavor and a reddish-brown color.

03:49:15.030 --> 03:49:17.830
Oyster sauce is made primarily from ground oysters.

03:49:18.560 --> 03:49:22.100
Sesame oil from roasted sesame seeds is a flavoring agent,

03:49:22.200 --> 03:49:25.000
and sesame paste is also a general flavoring agent.

03:49:25.650 --> 03:49:29.410
Star anise, which has a licorice-like flavor, and of course, soy sauce.

03:49:30.280 --> 03:49:32.240
Those are only seven different ingredients,

03:49:32.340 --> 03:49:35.360
but they should give you just about all the flavors that you need

03:49:35.360 --> 03:49:37.460
to give a dish a Chinese taste.

03:49:37.960 --> 03:49:40.380
Remember, though, you're not going to use them every day,

03:49:40.420 --> 03:49:42.020
so buy them in small quantities.

